<title>HONG KONG: New World Infra eases after placement.</title>
<headline>New World Infra eases after placement.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of New World Infrastructure Ltd fell on Wednesday after the China play raised more than HK$2.00 billion in a new share issue, brokers said.</p>
<p>The stock fell HK$0.95 to HK$24.10 in late morning trade.</p>
<p>New World Infrastructure parent New World Development Co Ltd placed 84 million existing shares at HK$24.30 on Tuesday and agreed to subscribe the same amount of new shares at the same price.</p>
<p>&quot;The placement price was at a five percent discount and this has put some pressure on the stock,&quot; said Charles Cheung, executive director at J &amp; A Securities.</p>
<p>But he said selling pressure was not too heavy.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
</text>
